# Slice 333: `fn: merge(f1, f2)` gives the receiver one Structure and no name. merge composes the parts of two created
# functions, which have no field name, and the name of the result is never taken from them (the author 2026-11-09: the
# missing argument name was a slip of the example, not an optional name): the application is refused where the
# traversal reaches it (the interpreter answers 5; native and forced code fail there).
fn: f1 (int: a) int
    return: a
end: f1
fn: f2 (int: a; int: b) int
int: r 1
fn: merge(f1, f2)
int: s 2
